# IntraCore: параметры HAL блока из базы STM32CubeMX (db/mcu/IP/*_Modes.xml).
# Порождено tools/hal_import — руками не править. Формат: src/Docs/Description/HalCatalogFormat.md
[Ip]
Name=DDR
Version=ddr_v1_0

[Parameters]
# имя|подпись|группа|единица|мин|макс|описание
CubeProgrammer_Minimal_Version|This is the minimal CubeProgrammer version for the concerned MPU package|||||
DDR_Start_Address|This is the base address for DDR subsystem in the specific MPU packages considered|||||
DDR_Frequency|DDR subsystem frequency|SYSTEM PARAMETERS|MHz|200|533|DDR subsystem frequency. This value is copied from the Clock Configuration panel
ADDRESS_MAPPING|Address Mapping configuration|SYSTEM PARAMETERS||||DDR Address mapping can be configured in RBC (Row-Bank-Column) or BRC (Bank-Row-Column)
RELAXED_TIMING_MODE|Relaxed Timing mode|SYSTEM PARAMETERS||||Add one supplementary clock cycle to some key DDR parameters. This ease the DDR bring-up by relaxing some key timings. The relaxed timing parameters are: tRC, tRCD and tRP. The +1 is made before register computation, thus not visible in the parameter edition interface
TEMPERATURE_OVER_85C|Temperature case over 85°C support|SYSTEM PARAMETERS||||DDR3 only, when TC > 85 TREFI = 3.9 and ASR = 1
IMPEDANCE_DURING_READ|Impedance During Read|SYSTEM PARAMETERS||||Changing Output impedance (DDR) and ODT (PHY) for read Operations.
IMPEDANCE_DURING_WRITE|Impedance During Write|SYSTEM PARAMETERS||||Changing Output impedance (PHY) and ODT (DDR) for write Operations.
SPEED_BIN_GRADE|Speed Bin Grade|SYSTEM PARAMETERS||||JEDEC Standard for DDR3 SDRAM. Set value of each timings from JEDEC standard for this 'Speed Bin Grade' selection. Tick 'Show Advanced Parameters' to see the involved timings. Select Speed Bin / Grade combination according to the DDR you have provisioned. In case your Speed Bin / Grade is not listed, please use: "1066G / 8-8-8” as a relaxed configuration that should work with most of DDRs. "1066E / 6-6-6” if you have faster DDR Speed Bin / Grade”
SCHEDULING_AND_QOS|Performance and scheduling|SYSTEM PARAMETERS||||Allows to choose the best scheduling and Quality of Service configuration for the targeted project. The various configurations possible are: - CONFIG 0: 1 port + No VPR/VPW + antistarvation - CONFIG 1: 2 ports + No VPR/VPW + antistarvation - CONFIG 2: 2 ports + QoS VPR/VPW + antistarvation - CONFIG 3: 2 ports + QoS VPR/VPW + timeout + antistarvation - CONFIG 4: 2 ports + QoS VPR/VPW + timeout + antistarvation - CONFIG 5: 1 port + intelligent percharge + No VPR/VPW + antistarvation
BL|Burst Length (BL)|SYSTEM PARAMETERS||||Burst Length (BL) is variable for LPDDR2. Fixed for other DDR types. Possible values are 4, 8 and 16.
CL|CAS Latency (CL)|JEDEC CORE TIMINGS|clocks|||The number of cycles between sending a column address to the memory and the beginning of the data in response. This is the number of cycles it takes to read the first bit of memory from a DRAM with the correct row already open. Unlike the other numbers, this is not a maximum, but an exact number that must be agreed on between the memory controller and the memory
CWL|CAS Write Latency (CWL)|JEDEC CORE TIMINGS|clocks|||"CAS Write Latency is the delay, in clock cycles, between the internal Write command and the availability of the first bit of input data.
tRAS|Row Active Time (tRAS)|JEDEC CORE TIMINGS|ns|0.01|150|ACT to PRE command period the minimum number of clock cycles required between a row active command and issuing the precharge command. This is the time needed to internally refresh the row, and overlaps with TRCD. In SDRAM modules, it is simply TRCD + CL. Otherwise, approximately equal to TRCD + 2×CL.
tMRD|MODE REGISTER SET command cycle time (tMRD)|COMMAND AND ADDRESS TIMINGS|ns|0.01|150|Mode Register Set command cycle time
tMOD|MODE REGISTER SET command update delay (tMOD)|COMMAND AND ADDRESS TIMINGS|ns|0.01|10000|Mode Register Set command update delay. This parameter can be found expressed in ns in the DRAM datasheet. Tools requires a conversion to clk. Please make sure you use your target DDR clock value for conversion.
tRCD|Row Address to column Address Delay (tRCD)|JEDEC CORE TIMINGS|ns|0.01|77|Activate to Read/Write command period: the minimum number of clock cycles required between opening a row of memory and accessing columns within it. The time to read the first bit of memory from a DRAM without an active row is TRCD + CL
tRP|Row Precharge Time (tRP)|JEDEC CORE TIMINGS|ns|0.01|58|PRE command period: the minimum number of clock cycles required between issuing the precharge command and opening the next row. The time to read the first bit of memory from a DRAM with the wrong row open is TRP + TRCD + CL
tRPab|Row Precharge Time (tRPab)|JEDEC CORE TIMINGS|ns|0.01|77|Row Precharge Time (all banks)
WL|Write Latency (WL)|JEDEC CORE TIMINGS|clocks|||The Write Latency is defined from the rising edge of the clock on which the Write Command is issued to the rising edge of the clock from which the tDQSS delay is measured.
tWR|Write recovery time (tWR)|JEDEC CORE TIMINGS|ns|0.01|255|Write to Precharge Delay / Write Recovery Time or tWR: This sets the number of clock cycles between the completion of a valid write operation and before an active bank can be precharged. Write to precharge formula is tCL -1 +(Burst Legnth / 2)+tWTR
tCCD|CAS#-to-CAS# command delay (tCCD)|COMMAND AND ADDRESS TIMINGS|clocks|1|7|CAS# to CAS#, min between 2 READ or 2 WRITE (burst can’tbe interrupted with DDR3)
tMRW|CAS#-to-CAS# command delay (tMRW)|JEDEC CORE TIMINGS|clocks|1|10|MR write command period
tMRR|CAS#-to-CAS# command delay (tMRR)|JEDEC CORE TIMINGS|clocks|1|7|MR read command period
tRRD|ACTIVATE-to-ACTIVATE minimum command period (tRRD)|COMMAND AND ADDRESS TIMINGS|ns|0.01|37|Activate to Activate delay or tRRD: Number of clock cycles between the activation of two rows in different banks of the same rank. (not much of a performance boost). This parameter can be found expressed in ns in the DRAM datasheet. Tools requires a conversion to clk. Please make sure you use your target DDR clock value for conversion.
tCKSRX|Min clocks before self refresh exit (tCKSRX)|SELF REFRESH TIMINGS|ns|1|15|Valid Clock Requirement before Self Refresh Exit (SRX) or Power-Down Exit (PDX) or Reset Exit. This parameter can be found expressed in ns in the DRAM datasheet. Tools requires a conversion to clk. Please make sure you use your target DDR clock value for conversion.
tCKSRE|Min clocks after self refresh entry (tCKSRE)|SELF REFRESH TIMINGS|ns|1|15|Valid Clock Requirement after Self Refresh Entry (SRE) or Power-Down Entry (PDE). This parameter can be found expressed in ns in the DRAM datasheet. Tools requires a conversion to clk. Please make sure you use your target DDR clock value for conversion.
tCKE|Min number of CKE high/low during Self Refresh and Power Down (tCKE)|POWER DOWN TIMINGS|ns|0.01|150|CKE minimum pulse width. This parameter can be found expressed in ns in the DRAM datasheet. Tools requires a conversion to clk. Please make sure you use your target DDR clock value for conversion.
tCKESR|Min CKE low between during SR (tCKESR)|JEDEC CORE TIMINGS|ns|0.01|150|CKE minimum pulse width during SELF REFRESH (low pulse width during SELF REFRESH)
tXP|Power-Down Exit (tXP)|POWER DOWN TIMINGS|ns|0.01|77|Exit Power Down with DLL on to any valid command; Exit Precharge Power Down with DLL frozen to commands not requiring a locked DLL. This parameter can be found expressed in ns in the DRAM datasheet. Tools requires a conversion to clk. Please make sure you use your target DDR clock value for conversion.
tDQSCKmax|Maximum DQS output access time (tDQSCKmax)|READ PARAMETERS|ns|0.01|18|DQS, DQS# rising edge output access time from rising CK, CK# - max value
tDQSCKmin|Minimum DQS output access time (tDQSCKmin)|READ PARAMETERS|ns|0.01|18|DQS, DQS# rising edge output access time from rising CK, CK# - min value
tXPDLL|Power-Down Exit (tXPDLL)|POWER DOWN TIMINGS|ns|0.01|100|Exit Precharge Power Down with DLL frozen to commands requiring a locked DLL. This parameter can be found expressed in ns in the DRAM datasheet. Tools requires a conversion to clk. Please make sure you use your target DDR clock value for conversion.
tRFC|Refresh Cycle Time (tRFC)|JEDEC CORE TIMINGS|ns|0.01|10000|Refresh to Activate Delay / Refresh Cycle Time or tRFC: Sets the number of clock cycles from the refresh command until the first activate command to the same rank.
tRFCab|Refresh Cycle time (tRFCab)|REFRESH PARAMETERS|ns|0.01|255|Minimum time from refresh to refresh or activate, if using all-bank refreshes
tXS|Exit SR to CMD not requiring locked DLL: = max(5 clk , tRFC +10ns) (tXS)|SELF REFRESH TIMINGS|ns|1|1023|Exit SR to CMD not requiring locked DLL: = max(5 clk , tRFC +10ns)
tXSDLL|Exit self refresh to commands requiring a locked DLL (tXSDLL)|SELF REFRESH TIMINGS|clocks|1|1023|Exit Self Refresh to commands requiring a locked DLL
RL|Read Latency (RL)|JEDEC CORE TIMINGS|clocks|||The Read Latency is defined from the rising edge of the clock on which the Read Command is issued to the rising edge of the clock from which the tDQSCK delay is measured.
wr2pre|Min WR to PRE in same bank (wr2pre)|DDR CONTROLLER TIMINGS|ns|0|0x7F|
wr2rd|Min write CMD to read CMD (wr2rd)|DDR CONTROLLER TIMINGS|clocks|0|0x3F|
rd2wr|Min read CMD to write CMD (rd2wr)|DDR CONTROLLER TIMINGS|clocks|0|0x3F|
read_latency|read CMD to read Data (read_latency)|DDR CONTROLLER TIMINGS|clocks|0|0x3F|
write_latency|Write CMD to write Data (write_latency)|DDR CONTROLLER TIMINGS|clocks|0|0x3F|
t_rc|Min between activate to same ban (t_rc), this parameter can be relaxed|DDR CONTROLLER TIMINGS||0|0x7F|
t_mrw|Time to wait after MRW or MRR (t_mrw)|DDR CONTROLLER TIMINGS|clocks|0|0x3FF|
t_mod|Load mode to non load mode (t_mod)|DDR CONTROLLER TIMINGS||0|0x3FF|
t_mrd|Mode Register Set to Mode Register Set (t_mrd)|DDR CONTROLLER TIMINGS||0|0x3F|
t_rcd|Mode Register Set to Mode Register Set (t_rcd), this parameter can be relaxed|DDR CONTROLLER TIMINGS||0|0x1F|
t_ccd|Min between 2 read or 2 write (t_ccd)|DDR CONTROLLER TIMINGS||0|0xF|
t_rrd|Min between Active to 2 banks (t_rrd)|DDR CONTROLLER TIMINGS||0|0xF|
t_faw|Four activate window (t_faw)|DDR CONTROLLER TIMINGS|ns|0|0x3F|
tFAW|Four ACTIVATE windows (tFAW)|COMMAND AND ADDRESS TIMINGS|ns|0.01|150|Four Activate Window or tFAW: The number of cycles in which four activates are allowed within the same rank.
tRASmax|Max between ACT and PRE to same bank in 1024 clk (tRASmax)|COMMAND AND ADDRESS TIMINGS|tREFI|1|31|Max between ACT and PRE to same bank in 1024 clk: 9 *tREFI
tRTP|READ-to-PRECHARGE time (tRTP)|COMMAND AND ADDRESS TIMINGS|ns|0.01|72|Read to Precharge delay or tRTP: The number of clock cycles between a read command to a row pre-charge command of the same rank. This parameter can be found expressed in ns in the DRAM datasheet. Tools requires a conversion to clk. Please make sure you use your target DDR clock value for conversion.
tRC|Row Cycle Time (tRC)|JEDEC CORE TIMINGS|ns|0.01|240|Row Cycle Time or tRC:This sets the number of cpu cycles a memory row (Remeber that memory is devided into "cells" much like an excel spredsheet) takes to complete a full cycle. A full cycle is from row activation to precharging of the active row. This setting has major affect on memory speed w/ a lower timing being faster. tRC= tras + tRP
tREFI|Refresh Interval Time (tREFI)|JEDEC CORE TIMINGS|us|||Refresh Mode Select / Refresh Period or tREFi: Sets the number of clock cycles refreshes. 3,9us (DDR TcMax above 85°C) or 7,8us (DDR TcMax 85°C).
tWTR|Write recovery time (tWTR)|COMMAND AND ADDRESS TIMINGS|ns|0.01|135|Delay from start of internal write transaction to internal read command. This parameter can be found expressed in ns in the DRAM datasheet. Tools requires a conversion to clk. Please make sure you use your target DDR clock value for conversion.
t_ras_max|Max between ACT and PRE to same bank in 1024 clk (t_ras_max)|DDR CONTROLLER TIMINGS||0|0x7F|
t_ras_min|Min between ACT and PRE (t_ras_min)|DDR CONTROLLER TIMINGS||0|0x7F|
t_xp|Exit Power Down (t_xp)|DDR CONTROLLER TIMINGS||0|0x1F|
t_rd2pre|Min RD to PRE in same bank (t_rd2pre)|DDR CONTROLLER TIMINGS||0|0x1F|
t_rp|PRECHARGE command period (t_rp), this parameter can be relaxed|DDR CONTROLLER TIMINGS||0|0x1F|
t_cksrx|Min clock stable before self refresh exit (t_cksrx)|DDR CONTROLLER TIMINGS|ns|0|0xF|
t_cksre|min clock stable after self refresh entry (t_cksre)|DDR CONTROLLER TIMINGS|ns|0|0xF|
t_ckesr|Min CKE low SR / Power down (t_ckesr)|DDR CONTROLLER TIMINGS|clocks|0|0x3F|
t_cke|CKE minimum pulse width (t_cke)|DDR CONTROLLER TIMINGS|clocks|0|0x3F|
t_ckdpde|Clock disable delay after DPDN (t_ckdpde)|DDR CONTROLLER TIMINGS|clocks|0|0xF|
t_ckdpdx|Clock stable time before DPDX (t_ckdpdx)|DDR CONTROLLER TIMINGS|clocks|0|0xF|
t_ckcsx|Clock stable time before next command after Clock Stop Exit (t_ckcsx)|DDR CONTROLLER TIMINGS|clocks|0|0xF|
t_ckpde|Clock disable delay after Enter Power-down (t_ckpde)|DDR CONTROLLER TIMINGS|clocks|0|0xF|
t_ckpdx|Clock stable time before Exit Power-down (t_ckpdx)|DDR CONTROLLER TIMINGS|clocks|0|0xF|
t_xs_dll_x32|Exit SR to CMD requiring locked DLL (t_xs_dll_x32)|||0|0x7F|
t_xs_x32|Exit Self Refresh to CMD not requiring locked DLL (t_xs_x32)|DDR CONTROLLER TIMINGS|clocks|0|0x7F|
t_xsr|Exit self refresh to any command (t_xsr)|DDR CONTROLLER TIMINGS||0|0xFFF|
t_rfc_nom_x1_x32|tREFI in multiple of 32 clocks (t_rfc_nom_x1_x32)|DDR CONTROLLER TIMINGS||0|0xFFF|
t_rfc_min|Refresh Control (t_rfc_min)|DDR CONTROLLER TIMINGS|clocks|0|0x3FF|
wr_odt_hold|Cycle to hold ODT for Write, min 2 recommended (wr_odt_hold)|DDR CONTROLLER TIMINGS|clocks|0|0xF|
wr_odt_delay|ODT delay should be set to 0 for DDR3 (wr_odt_delay)|DDR CONTROLLER TIMINGS|clocks|0|0x1F|
rd_odt_hold|Cycle to hold ODT for Read min 2 recommended (rd_odt_hold)|DDR CONTROLLER TIMINGS|clocks|0|0xF|
rd_odt_delay|ODT delay should be set to CL-CWL for DDR3 (rd_odt_delay)|DDR CONTROLLER TIMINGS|clocks|0|0x1F|
