0dqdly7|Byte lane 0 – DQ delay for bit 7 fine tuning (both DQS/DQS# clock)|BYTE 0||||This parameter contains the DQ bit lane fine delay after tuning. Default value is 0x0F. Valid settings for each 2-bit control field are: 0 stands for 0 (DQ=00 DQ#=00 0000(0)) (nominal delay) 5 stands for 1 (DQ=01 DQ#=01 0101(5)) (nominal delay + 1 step) A stands for 2 (DQ=10 DQ#=10 1010(A)) (nominal delay + 2 steps) F stands for 3 (DQ=11 DQ#=11 1111(F)) (nominal delay + 3 steps) Please use the DDR Tuning feature of STM32CubeMx DDR Test Suite to get tuned values for your hardware design.
